          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %em analysis
            usually refers to any of a broad family of fields that deals with a general theory of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limits
            in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} convergence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            (or more generally of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus"} calculus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+calculus"}> differential calculus
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+calculus"}> integral calculus
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            and
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real number system
            is describable as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+space"} complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordered+field"} ordered field
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
            functions allow to formalize concepts like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} convergence
            in terms of existence of sufficiently small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epsilontic+analysis"} epsilontic analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            of metric spaces, and this way the field of analysis has a large overlap with the field of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            and the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
          %p
            Analysis can also refer to other responses to the problem of founding these developments, especially “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+analysis"}> infinitesimal analysis
            ” which admits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+quantities"} infinitesimal quantities
            not found in the classical real number system and which takes various forms, for example the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonstandard+analysis"} nonstandard analysis
            first introduced by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abraham+Robinson"} Abraham Robinson
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential analysis
